Based on the screenshots and your report, the image is being “pulled out” of your arbitrary Pandoc `Div` block by Quarto’s post‐processor in `applyStretch()`.  In revealjs mode, if there is exactly one image on a slide, Quarto will auto‐add an `r-stretch` class and then move that image up to be a direct child of `<section>`.  That logic correctly avoids moving images inside a `.column` (so Slide B works), but does *not* avoid images inside arbitrary `<div>` blocks (so Slides A & C move outside).

The simplest fix is to only perform the “lift‐up” when the image really *is* already a direct child of the slide (or at least in a top‐level node equal to the slide), i.e. don’t move images that live inside custom `<div>` blocks.  In `src/format/reveal/format-reveal.ts`, locate the relocation `if` in `applyStretch()` and add a check that the first‐level container is the slide itself:

